The '''[[1987–88 NBA season|1987]] [[NBA draft]]''' was held on June 22, 1987, in New York City.

This draft included two future members of the [[NBA 50 Greatest Players]] list, [[David Robinson]] and [[Scottie Pippen]], as well as fellow Hall of Famer [[Reggie Miller]], who was named to the [[NBA 75th Anniversary Team]]. Other notable selections include [[Kevin Johnson (basketball player)|Kevin Johnson]], [[Kenny Smith]],  [[Horace Grant]],  [[Reggie Lewis]], [[Muggsy Bogues]], [[Mark Jackson (basketball)|Mark Jackson]], and [[Šarūnas Marčiulionis]].  Also in this draft was former [[University of Florida|Florida Gators]] men's basketball head coach [[Billy Donovan]] (drafted 68th by the [[Utah Jazz]]), who led that program to NCAA Division I Men's Basketball Championships in [[2006 in sports|2006]] and in [[2007 in sports|2007]].

David Robinson did not join the NBA until the [[1989–90 NBA season|1989–90 season]] due to his service commitment with the [[United States Navy]]. This was the last NBA draft to go over three rounds, as it was reduced to three next year and later to two since 1989.

